# A method that an object literal holds in a field, called on a receiver that is only expected to have the layout. That the field is filled may become true again, so a test of the receiver in front of the call says nothing about the read:
# the function that was read is tested, whatever is expected of it, and under the tests of the read that test is about a closure just made
# The functions are checked functions of the program, where the copy goes on behind the stretch. Behind layouts that nobody has checked it holds the stretch alone: place-type-tests-copies-in-checked-functions-are-rare.ir
